 "assumptions": [
  "Sun azimuth and elevation are the stored JPL Horizons apparent values for each site (airless body, no refraction). Azimuth is clockwise from local true north.",
  "Panel tilt is the angle between the panel normal and the local vertical on the reference sphere (0° horizontal, 90° vertical). Local surface slope is not applied.",
  "Fixed panel: constant tilt and azimuth for the whole window. When no azimuth is given, one azimuth per site is chosen with hindsight to maximise the geometric-horizon index (1° grid) and reused for every horizon type and bound.",
  "Azimuth tracking: the panel rotates about the local vertical and always faces the Sun's azimuth at a constant tilt. Dual-axis: the panel always faces the Sun.",
  "The Sun is a uniform disc of nominal radius 0.2666° cut by a straight horizon; limb darkening and the ±1.7 % seasonal change in apparent radius are ignored.",
  "Each sample holds for min(step, end − t) hours (sample-and-hold over [start_utc, end_utc)); a sample at the window end has zero weight.",
  "Only direct sunlight is considered: no earthshine, no light reflected from terrain, no self-shading by the lander or by neighbouring panels."
 ],
