   "description": "Relative incidence index derived from the stored Sun azimuth/elevation and per-epoch visibility states; no new ephemeris request.",
   "version": "7b.1"
  }
 ],
 "limitations": [
  "This is geometry only. It is not irradiance and not electrical output: Sun distance, cell efficiency, panel area, temperature, dust, degradation and storage are not modelled.",
  "Temporal sampling: the Sun's azimuth moves about 0.5° per hour at the lunar poles and the state is held constant between samples, so changes shorter than the 60-minute step are not resolved.",
  "Sites are comparable only within this analysis (same window and step). A site is reported as leading only when its minimum exceeds every other site's maximum by more than 0.5 percentage points; overlapping or closer values do not support a ranking.",
  "A range (minimum to maximum) is not a probability distribution; no value inside it is more likely than another.",
  "GEOMETRIC analysis: the horizon is the smooth 0° lunar sphere. Terrain shadowing is not modelled, so real illumination at polar sites can be far lower. No terrain-aware value is reported."
 ]
